00:32:07.000 --> 00:33:07.000
All the women were tourists and had their clothing from the waist down removed. It was believed Joe and her daughters were lured into a boat in a manner similar to that of Lucy, hence why their car was at the ramp. A behavior analysis of the Rogers killer conducted by the FBI aligned with Dave Posner. They had described the killer as intelligent with good social skills. He was adept at making people feel at ease while presenting himself as a regular and hard-working, law-abiding citizen. His crimes would come as a surprise to those who knew him. Due to the killer's familiarity with the area and the fact he owned a boat, he most certainly lived in Tampa. The FBI believed Joe, Michelle and Christie were not his first victims and that he would strike again.
所有受害者都是游客，且腰部以下的衣物都被脱掉了。据信，乔和她的女儿们是以类似于露西的方式被诱骗上船的，这就是为什么她们的车会停在坡道上。联邦调查局对罗杰斯案凶手的行为分析与戴夫·波斯纳相吻合。他们将凶手描述为聪明且社交能力强的人。他善于让人们感到放松，同时表现得像一个普通、勤奋、守法的公民。他的罪行会让那些认识他的人感到震惊。由于凶手对该地区很熟悉，且拥有一艘船，他几乎肯定住在坦帕。联邦调查局认为，乔、米歇尔和克里斯蒂并不是他的第一批受害者，而且他还会再次作案。

39
00:33:07.000 --> 00:34:18.000
Locating Dave Posner became a high priority. Detectives weighed up the risk of tracking Dave down versus the chance he'd flee if he knew they were coming for him. The crimes were too significant to take a reserved approach, so officers decided to circulate the composite sketch of Dave in local newspapers in the hopes someone would recognize him. Saturday, November 4, 1989, was five months to the day Joe, Michelle and Christie Rogers left for their fateful trip to Florida. Tampa resident Joanne Steffi was sitting at her kitchen table reading the paper. The Rogers case was being spotlighted once again as a composite sketch of a possible suspect was now available. Joanne read about the case but had to set the paper aside upon realizing she was running late for an appointment. As she drove along her street, Joanne passed the home belonging to her creepy neighbor, locally known as Obi.
找到戴夫·波斯纳成了当务之急。侦探们权衡了追踪戴夫的风险与他得知消息后逃跑的可能性。这些罪行太严重了，不能采取保守的方法，因此警官们决定在当地报纸上发布戴夫的模拟画像，希望有人能认出他。1989年11月4日星期六，距离乔、米歇尔和克里斯蒂·罗杰斯踏上前往佛罗里达的致命之旅正好五个月。坦帕居民乔安妮·斯特菲正坐在厨房桌旁看报纸。罗杰斯案再次成为焦点，因为现在有了嫌疑人的模拟画像。乔安妮读了关于此案的报道，但因为赶时间去赴约，不得不放下报纸。当她开车经过自己所在的街道时，经过了她那位令人毛骨悚然的邻居的家，当地人称他为“奥比”。

40
00:34:18.000 --> 00:35:16.000
It suddenly dawned on her. Obi resembled the suspect sketch in the Rogers homicide case. She also drove a dark colored car and owned a blue and white power boat. Joanne clipped the suspect sketch out of the paper and showed it to her friend and fellow neighbor, a woman named Moselle. Moselle warned Joanne not to implicate Obi unless Joanne was absolutely certain of her theory. Joanne agreed and took the clipping home where she stuck it to her fridge. It remained there until early the following year when Joanne happened to spot Obi watching her house from the street one night. Scared of what Obi might have been capable of, Joanne spoke to a deputy sheriff who said he would look into it.
她突然意识到，奥比长得和罗杰斯谋杀案中的嫌疑人画像很像。他也开着一辆深色的车，并拥有一艘蓝白相间的动力艇。乔安妮从报纸上剪下嫌疑人画像，给她的朋友兼邻居莫塞尔看。莫塞尔警告乔安妮，除非有绝对把握，否则不要指控奥比。乔安妮同意了，把剪报带回家贴在冰箱上。直到第二年年初，乔安妮有一天晚上偶然发现奥比在街上盯着她的房子看，剪报才一直贴在那里。因为害怕奥比可能做出的事，乔安妮告诉了一位副警长，对方说会调查此事。

41
00:35:16.000 --> 00:36:15.000
Joanne passed with no news, leading Joanne to assume authorities had investigated Obi and cleared him of any involvement in the Rogers case. Two years passed without any breakthroughs. In October 1991, a Florida-based police sergeant named Glenn Moore joined the team investigating the Rogers case. It was hoped a fresh pair of eyes might uncover something previously missed. Moore and the team went over all the information they had. Their attention soon turned to a brochure that was found in the Rogers family car. It was for Clearwater Beach, a popular coastal resort about 15 miles from Tampa. The brochure was found to have originated from a tourist stop near the Georgia-Florida border.
乔安妮一直没有收到消息，这让她以为当局已经调查了奥比并排除了他与罗杰斯案的任何关联。两年过去了，没有任何突破。1991年10月，一位名叫格伦·摩尔的佛罗里达州警长加入了罗杰斯案的调查组。人们希望换个角度看问题可能会发现之前遗漏的东西。摩尔和团队重新梳理了所有信息。他们的注意力很快转向了在罗杰斯家车里发现的一本小册子。那是关于克利尔沃特海滩的，这是一个距离坦帕约15英里的热门沿海度假胜地。这本小册子被发现源自佐治亚州和佛罗里达州边界附近的一个旅游站点。

42
00:36:15.000 --> 00:37:05.000
Anyone linked to the brochure and distribution had already been questioned and cleared. The brochure featured handwritten directions to the Rogers Tampa-based hotel. Whoever scrawled them had a very distinct writing style. They put capital letters among the lower case and their letter Y had a uniquely long tail. This peaked Sergeant Moore's interest. The handwriting did not match Jo's, Michelle's or Christie's. Sergeant Moore pondered the likelihood that Joanne and the girls got lost en route to the days in and had asked someone for directions. The brochure was checked for prints revealing a partial palm print that didn't belong to any of the three Rogers women.
任何与这本小册子及其分发有关的人都已接受过询问并被排除嫌疑。小册子上写着手写的去往罗杰斯在坦帕入住酒店的路线。写下这些字的人笔迹非常独特。他们在小写字母中夹杂了大写字母，而且字母“Y”的尾巴特别长。这引起了摩尔警长的兴趣。笔迹与乔、米歇尔或克里斯蒂的都不符。摩尔警长推测，乔安妮和女孩们在去酒店的路上迷路了，并向某人问路。小册子经过指纹检查，发现了一个不属于三名罗杰斯女性中任何一人的部分掌纹。

43
00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:47.000
Sergeant Moore came up with a novel idea. He had the handwriting from the brochure printed in newspapers and posted on billboards in the Tampa area. It was accompanied with the message. Who wrote these directions? You may know who killed the Rogers family. A $25,000 reward was also on offer as an added incentive. Joanne Steffie saw the handwriting sample in the local paper and took it to her friend, Moselle. Moselle had been listening to Joanne's worries about their neighbour, Obie, for some time.
摩尔警长想出了一个新颖的主意。他将小册子上的笔迹印在报纸上，并张贴在坦帕地区的广告牌上。随附的信息是：“谁写了这些路线？你可能知道是谁杀害了罗杰斯一家。”作为额外的激励，还提供了2.5万美元的悬赏。乔安妮·斯特菲在当地报纸上看到了笔迹样本，并把它拿给朋友莫塞尔看。莫塞尔已经听乔安妮倾诉关于邻居奥比的担忧有一段时间了。

44
00:37:47.000 --> 00:38:34.000
Obie was an aluminium salesman who had previously provided Moselle with a quote for work she wanted done to her front porch. He had written out an estimate and given her a carbon copy. Moselle searched for hours and eventually found the estimate buried among paperwork. She and Joanne compared it to the sample in the newspaper article. It was an exact match. Joanne mailed and faxed it to the local police headquarters. She then waited to hear on the news that Obie, whose real name was Oba Chandler, had been arrested in relation to the Rogers triple homicide. She heard nothing.
奥比是一名铝材推销员，曾为莫塞尔想要做的前廊工程提供过报价。他写了一份估价单，并给了她一份复写件。莫塞尔找了几个小时，终于在文件堆中找到了那份估价单。她和乔安妮将其与报纸文章中的样本进行了对比。完全吻合。乔安妮将其邮寄并传真给了当地警察总部。然后她等待着在新闻中听到奥比（真名奥巴·钱德勒）因涉及罗杰斯三尸命案而被捕的消息。但她什么也没听到。

45
00:38:34.000 --> 00:39:31.000
Joanne made several follow-up calls to find out if the police could analyse the handwriting samples she had sent. She was told that the case investigators were making their way through a large amount of leads and that hers would be examined in time. June passed and by late July, Joanne was still awaiting contact from authorities. Frustrated by their lack of action, Moselle's adult daughter faxed the handwriting samples through to police again. Her accompanying message read, Here is another copy of Oba Chandler's handwriting. Many of us are convinced that his handwriting is the one published in the papers. We feel so strongly that they are one and the same that due to your lack of response, we were tempted to pursue this with a handwriting expert of our own.
乔安妮打了几个后续电话，询问警方是否可以分析她寄去的笔迹样本。她被告知案件调查人员正在处理大量线索，她的样本会及时进行检查。六月过去了，到了七月下旬，乔安妮仍在等待当局的联系。由于对他们的不作为感到沮丧，莫塞尔的成年女儿再次将笔迹样本传真给了警方。随附的信息写道：“这是奥巴·钱德勒笔迹的另一份副本。我们许多人都确信他的笔迹就是报纸上公布的那一份。我们非常确信它们是同一个人所写，由于你们一直没有回应，我们打算找我们自己的笔迹专家来处理这件事。”

46
00:39:31.000 --> 00:40:27.000
Following this, investigators were willing to take on the concerns of Joanne's Steffi and her neighbours. Within three days, a handwriting expert confirmed that the directions on the Clearwater Beach brochure were indeed penned by Oba Chandler. It was such a close match, it was regarded as unmistakable. While this only proved that Chandler had given the Rogers women directions, it established that he had direct contact with them in the lead-up to their murders. And he knew where they were staying. Yet, by the time police closed in on Oba Chandler, they were too late. He was long gone. Oba Chandler was born in Ohio, the only son in a family of five children.
此后，调查人员愿意接受乔安妮的斯蒂芬妮及其邻居们的担忧。三天内，一位笔迹专家证实，清水海滩宣传册上的方向指引确实是奥巴·钱德勒亲笔所写。由于匹配度极高，这被认为是无可辩驳的。虽然这仅证明了钱德勒曾为罗杰斯一家指路，但它确立了他在她们遇害前与她们有过直接接触的事实。而且他知道她们住在哪里。然而，当警方锁定奥巴·钱德勒时，已经太晚了。他早已逃之夭夭。奥巴·钱德勒出生于俄亥俄州，是家中五个孩子里唯一的儿子。

47
00:40:27.000 --> 00:41:16.000
His father was a strict disciplinarian who took his own life. The death marked a turning point in 10-year-old Oba Chandler. The once quiet and intelligent boy became disruptive. This carried on into his adult years, during which Chandler served short stints in jail for armed robbery, drug dealing and counterfeiting. While committing a home invasion, Chandler forced the female resident to undress before restraining her to a bed. On another occasion, he bound a woman's hands and feet and covered her mouth in duct tape. By May 1988, Chandler was in the midst of his third marriage. He had eight children with multiple women.
他的父亲是一位严厉的管教者，后来选择了自杀。这次死亡标志着10岁的奥巴·钱德勒人生的转折点。曾经安静聪明的男孩变得具有破坏性。这种行为一直持续到他成年，期间钱德勒因武装抢劫、贩毒和伪造货币多次入狱。在一次入室抢劫中，钱德勒强迫女住户脱光衣服，然后将她捆绑在床上。另一次，他捆绑了一名女性的手脚，并用胶带封住了她的嘴。到1988年5月，钱德勒正处于他的第三段婚姻中。他与多名女性育有八个孩子。

48
00:41:16.000 --> 00:42:23.000
Chandler purchased a small bungalow-style home in Tampa. His blue and white powerboat was docked at the pier connected to his property and he parked his dark-colored Jeep Cherokee in the driveway. Oba Chandler worked hard to build a good rapport with his neighbors. Then, in June 1990, he surprised them all by suddenly moving away without telling anyone. It was a year into the Rogers Homicide Investigation and shortly after a composite sketch of the suspect was widely publicised. The investigation into Oba Chandler was given the codename The Tin Man, in reference to Chandler's work as an aluminium salesman. Detectives flew to Ontario in Canada where they spoke with Lucy, the woman who was raped aboard a boat by Dave Posner in May 1989. Upon viewing a photo lineup, Lucy pointed out Oba Chandler as being Dave Posner.
钱德勒在坦帕买了一栋小型平房。他的蓝白相间动力艇停泊在自家房产相连的码头上，他将深色的吉普切诺基停在车道上。奥巴·钱德勒努力与邻居建立良好的关系。然而，1990年6月，他突然搬走，没有告诉任何人，这让所有人都感到惊讶。当时罗杰斯谋杀案调查已经进行了一年，就在嫌疑人的合成素描被广泛公布后不久。针对奥巴·钱德勒的调查代号为“锡人”，这是指钱德勒作为铝材推销员的工作。侦探们飞往加拿大安大略省，与露西交谈，她曾于1989年5月在船上被戴夫·波斯纳强奸。在查看照片排查时，露西指认奥巴·钱德勒就是戴夫·波斯纳。

49
00:42:23.000 --> 00:43:22.000
The friend who had been travelling with Lucy at the time made the same identification. Chandler's resemblance to the composite sketch of Lucy's rapist was uncanny. Oba Chandler was tracked almost 300 miles from Tampa. He had resettled on the other side of the state in the seaside city of Daytona Beach. On Thursday, September 24, 1992, Chandler was visiting pawn shops trying to offload $750,000 worth of jewellery he had stolen. When he pulled into a gas station, officers swooped and he was placed under arrest for sexual battery. Word of his arrest spread, along with rumours that he was involved in the murders of Joe, Michelle and Christie Rogers. The news left his current neighbours in Daytona Beach stunned.
当时与露西同行的朋友也做出了同样的指认。钱德勒与露西强奸案嫌疑人的合成素描长得惊人地相似。奥巴·钱德勒在距离坦帕近300英里外的地方被追踪到。他已搬到州另一侧的海滨城市代托纳比奇重新定居。1992年9月24日星期四，钱德勒正在当铺试图脱手他偷来的价值75万美元的珠宝。当他驶入加油站时，警察一拥而上，他因性侵罪被捕。他被捕的消息传开了，同时还有传言称他卷入了乔、米歇尔和克里斯蒂·罗杰斯的谋杀案。这个消息让他在代托纳比奇的现任邻居们感到震惊。

50
00:43:22.000 --> 00:44:15.000
He seemed like a normal guy, one neighbour told the Tampa Times newspaper. With Oba Chandler behind bars, detectives worked to see if they could implicate him in the Rogers triple homicide. They were able to recover Chandler's old blue and white powerboat, which he had sold three months after the murders. So much time had passed, nothing of significance was uncovered. Yet, one of Chandler's sisters recalled him collecting newspaper clippings about the Rogers case. When she confronted him about it, he allegedly confessed to the killings, before saying, I'm just bullshitting. On another occasion, Chandler allegedly told one of his daughters that he couldn't go back to Florida because, quote,
“他看起来像个正常人，”一位邻居告诉《坦帕时报》。随着奥巴·钱德勒入狱，侦探们努力寻找证据，看能否将他与罗杰斯三尸命案联系起来。他们成功找回了钱德勒那艘旧的蓝白动力艇，他在谋杀案发生三个月后将其卖掉。由于时间过去太久，没有发现任何有价值的线索。然而，钱德勒的一位姐妹回忆说，他曾收集关于罗杰斯案的剪报。当她就此事质问他时，据称他承认了杀人，随后又说：“我只是在胡说八道。”另一次，钱德勒据称告诉他的一个女儿，他不能回佛罗里达，因为，引用：

51
00:44:15.000 --> 00:45:12.000
the police are looking for me because I killed some women. Chandler had also allegedly confessed to his son-in-law, saying he threw at least one woman overboard. The evidence against Oba Chandler was circumstantial, though it was enough for a grand jury to indict him to stand trial for the murders of Joe, Michelle and Christie Rogers in addition to his crimes against Lucy. Chandler rented her not guilty plea. The trial commenced in September 1994. Oba Chandler appeared in court wearing a casual shirt and khaki pants and flashing a broad smile. He was impassive throughout proceedings, but would become jovial with his defense team during breaks.
“警察在找我，因为我杀了一些女人。”据称钱德勒还向他的女婿坦白，说他至少把一个女人扔进了海里。针对奥巴·钱德勒的证据是间接的，但足以让大陪审团起诉他，就乔、米歇尔和克里斯蒂·罗杰斯的谋杀案以及针对露西的罪行进行审判。钱德勒拒不认罪。审判于1994年9月开始。奥巴·钱德勒出庭时穿着休闲衬衫和卡其裤，脸上挂着灿烂的笑容。他在整个诉讼过程中面无表情，但在休息期间会与辩护团队谈笑风生。

52
00:45:12.000 --> 00:46:10.000
The prosecution relied on similar fact evidence in the rape case of Canadian tourist Lucy to show that both crimes were linked. The assistant state attorney argued that the boat was the perfect place for Chandler to commit his crimes, saying, It could be committed in darkness and without the possibility of escape. Chandler's defense team put forth that acts between their client and Lucy were consensual. While they admitted that things got out of hand in that instance, they stressed that this didn't mean their client was a triple murderer. He didn't do it. It's that simple they maintained. They painted Chandler as a helpful man who had only offered the Rogers women directions. That simple act of kindness had now spiralled into wild and baseless accusations.
检方在加拿大游客露西的强奸案中依赖类似事实证据，以证明两起罪行有关联。助理州检察官辩称，船是钱德勒犯罪的完美场所，他说：“这可以在黑暗中进行，且没有逃脱的可能性。”钱德勒的辩护团队提出，他们当事人与露西之间的行为是双方自愿的。虽然他们承认在那次事件中事情失控了，但他们强调这并不意味着他们的当事人是三尸命案的凶手。“他没做过。就这么简单，”他们坚持道。他们将钱德勒描绘成一个乐于助人的人，只是为罗杰斯一家指了路。那种简单的善举现在演变成了疯狂且毫无根据的指控。

53
00:46:10.000 --> 00:47:12.000
Three men who spent time remanded with Oba Chandler were called to testify. One said that Chandler had told him the only reason he hadn't killed the Canadian tourist was because her friend back on shore would recognize him. Another testified that Chandler had told him that his biggest mistake was leaving the note in the car. Chandler had allegedly told another inmate that the last words he spoke to the Rogers women before throwing them overboard was to, quote, Swim for it. When it was looking likely that the jury would not find in Oba Chandler's favor, the defense threw a curveball. They argued that the sexual battery charge should be dropped as Lucy couldn't pinpoint exactly where the alleged rape had taken place. If it occurred more than nine nautical miles off the coast, it was outside of US jurisdiction.
三名曾与奥巴·钱德勒一起被拘留的男子被传唤作证。其中一人说，钱德勒告诉他，他没有杀害那名加拿大游客的唯一原因，是因为她在岸上的朋友会认出他。另一人作证说，钱德勒告诉他，他最大的错误是在车里留下了那张纸条。据称钱德勒告诉另一名囚犯，他在把罗杰斯一家扔进海里前说的最后一句话是，引用：“游回去吧。”当陪审团看起来不太可能做出对奥巴·钱德勒有利的裁决时，辩方抛出了一个杀手锏。他们辩称，性侵指控应该撤销，因为露西无法准确指出所谓的强奸发生在何处。如果发生在离岸九海里以外，那就超出了美国的司法管辖范围。

54
00:47:12.000 --> 00:48:08.000
This meant the prosecution would also lose their similar fact evidence tying Lucy's case to the Rogers. In response, the prosecution reiterated key details in Lucy's statement. Specifically, she saw people on the shore and heard a bell ringing from the mainland. This meant Chandler's boat must have been only around a mile offshore. The defense then sought to implicate John Rogers in the murders, given his previous sex offences against his niece Michelle Rogers. The defense floated the long since disregarded hitman theory to explain how John could pull off the crimes. This prompted the judge to respond, You are not getting into John Rogers. John Rogers is a red herring. That is a moot issue.
这意味着检方也将失去将露西案与罗杰斯案联系起来的类似事实证据。作为回应，检方重申了露西陈述中的关键细节。具体来说，她看到了岸上有人，并听到了来自大陆的钟声。这意味着钱德勒的船一定离岸只有一英里左右。辩方随后试图将约翰·罗杰斯牵连进谋杀案，鉴于他之前对侄女米歇尔·罗杰斯的性犯罪记录。辩方提出了早已被忽视的“职业杀手理论”来解释约翰如何能犯下这些罪行。这促使法官回应道：“你们不要扯到约翰·罗杰斯身上。约翰·罗杰斯是个干扰项。那是个无关紧要的问题。”

55
00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:58.000
